 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Decorator:** `needs_app_scope`, defined in `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It loads the app and pushes its app context before your callback runs.\n\nYou often don't need to apply it yourself:\n- A command registered with `@app.cli.command()` or `@bundle.cli.command()` is wrapped automatically, because `app.cli` (`src/tessel/app.py:338`) and `bundle.cli` (`src/tessel/bundles.py:49`) are `AppGroup`s. `AppGroup.command` (`src/tessel/cli.py:413`) applies `needs_app_scope` by default.\n- To opt out, pass `needs_app_scope=False`.\n- For a standalone `click` command or a custom `AppGroup('user')` (see `docs/cli.rst:346`), use `@needs_app_scope` directly on the callback.\n\n**Class that loads the app:** `LaunchInfo` (`src/tessel/cli.py:293`). Its `load_app()` (line 333) finds and caches the app. `needs_app_scope` calls it through `ctx.ensure_object(LaunchInfo).load_app()` (line 397). The top-level CLI group that dispatches commands is `TesselGroup` (`src/tessel/cli.py:531`). It also calls `info.load_app()` to list `app.cli` commands.",
